WEBVTT

00:00.940 --> 00:04.860
With over thirty million
players worldwide,

00:04.860 --> 00:07.390
it reigns supreme over
all Full-Dive VR games.

00:07.950 --> 00:11.490
In Shangri-La Frontier,
known as a god-tier game,

00:12.030 --> 00:12.660
THE SEVEN COLOSSI

00:12.660 --> 00:14.990
THE SEVEN COLOSSI
there exist Unique Monsters

00:14.990 --> 00:17.410
THE SEVEN COLOSSI
called "The Seven Colossi."

00:17.410 --> 00:18.000
THE SEVEN COLOSSI

00:18.460 --> 00:23.330
One of them is Lycagon the Nightslayer.

00:24.440 --> 00:27.050
I'm nothing like the last time!

00:28.050 --> 00:32.760
I'll show you the power
of a level-99 player!

00:49.150 --> 00:55.120
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:05.400 --> 02:09.980
#37: EMBRACING YOUR AMBITIONS
IN THE LIGHT PART 2

02:18.070 --> 02:22.120
Heh! This stinging sensation...
Sure brings back memories!

02:22.440 --> 02:23.530
Amazing.

02:23.530 --> 02:27.250
It's difficult to deflect Lycagon's attack
with light weapons.

02:27.250 --> 02:28.500
I'll join you!

02:32.130 --> 02:34.260
Supreme Divineslash!

02:34.260 --> 02:36.640
SUPREME DIVINESLASH

02:37.720 --> 02:38.590
So tough!

02:44.750 --> 02:47.520
I knew it.
Fighting her the normal way won't cut it.

02:47.910 --> 02:51.070
Rei! I'll keep her
focused on me for now!

02:51.730 --> 02:54.780
Once you heal up, look for a window
to strike a powerful attack!

02:54.780 --> 02:56.240
All right!

03:04.620 --> 03:06.080
It's her clone attack!

03:19.760 --> 03:22.640
This clone attack...

03:22.640 --> 03:26.270
I've seen a lot of it
during her fight with SF-Zoo.

03:26.770 --> 03:30.530
An ambush from a clone that can move from
shadow to shadow is certainly dangerous.

03:30.940 --> 03:35.110
But it looks like her clone
can only do simple actions.

03:35.110 --> 03:36.360
Simple actions?

03:36.950 --> 03:43.120
The clone's basic maneuvers were all
as simple as frontal lunging attacks.

03:43.120 --> 03:48.920
It never once did anything complex,
like pursuing a dodging target!

03:48.920 --> 03:50.130
Which means...

04:01.570 --> 04:04.930
If you watch the positions of shadows
cast by buildings and move accordingly,

04:04.930 --> 04:07.600
it's not impossible to
continually evade them!

04:07.600 --> 04:12.150
What we need to watch out for more
is the attack she used on Animalia.

04:18.180 --> 04:23.410
When the moon's hidden by the clouds,
the entire map will be treated as "dark,"

04:23.410 --> 04:27.120
and it'll be hard to tell exactly
where she will attack from!

04:27.620 --> 04:30.670
Moreover, her clone
will melt into the darkness,

04:30.670 --> 04:33.170
making it even harder to catch sight of!

04:33.170 --> 04:35.810
Frankly, it's close to impossible
to dodge them.

04:38.720 --> 04:43.430
For now, we've got to chip away at her
as much as possible while the moon's out!

04:44.140 --> 04:44.970
Rei!

04:45.330 --> 04:47.850
Watch how the clouds
are moving while you fight!

04:47.850 --> 04:49.600
R-Roger that!

04:54.190 --> 04:58.570
Not even Hizutome can attack her
while under that assault.

05:01.030 --> 05:03.820
I gotta deal as much damage as I can!

05:07.790 --> 05:09.160
Apocalypse!

05:09.750 --> 05:11.420
APOCALYPSE

05:16.130 --> 05:18.300
Whoa, that's a nice critical hit!

05:24.870 --> 05:28.310
Sunraku! I'll pull her attention this time!

05:28.310 --> 05:29.600
Roger!

05:30.980 --> 05:34.810
Next, I'll use Gilta Brille
to blow her a big time!

05:42.550 --> 05:45.780
This is my fourth time fighting Lycagon!

05:45.780 --> 05:47.700
I can at least grab her attention!

05:52.120 --> 05:54.830
Heh, the same ol' clone attack again?

05:57.160 --> 05:58.960
Whew, that was close!

05:58.960 --> 06:01.340
But once I dodge it, that's it!

06:01.340 --> 06:04.390
Sunraku! You've got it wrong! That is—

06:04.390 --> 06:05.390
What?

06:06.850 --> 06:08.140
The real one?!

06:11.100 --> 06:12.310
Sunraku!

06:20.570 --> 06:21.530
SHANA-OH POSSESSION
EMBODY THE POWER OF A NIMBLE HERO AND GREATLY

06:21.530 --> 06:22.570
SHANA-OH POSSESSION
INCREASES JUMPING ABILITY FOR A FIXED TIME

06:24.450 --> 06:27.530
Sunraku, good job
making out of that alive.

06:27.530 --> 06:30.080
Yeah, somehow.

06:30.910 --> 06:33.370
It would've killed me instantly
if I didn't have Inventoria.

06:39.750 --> 06:41.340
That attack just now...

06:41.800 --> 06:44.830
To think that the real one
can also traverse the shadows...

06:44.830 --> 06:50.350
Nah, that fact by itself
is not much of a surprise.

06:50.350 --> 06:51.270
Huh?

06:52.270 --> 06:55.870
The real issue is that
she was hiding that from us.

06:56.370 --> 06:57.610
I had assumed...

06:58.150 --> 07:00.520
That the real one can't
move through shadows.

07:00.520 --> 07:03.740
By not doing that even once
during the earlier fight...

07:04.240 --> 07:06.820
She made us believe that!

07:06.820 --> 07:07.740
No way!

07:08.180 --> 07:09.200
That means...

07:09.620 --> 07:12.370
From the moment she was fighting SF-Zoo,

07:12.370 --> 07:15.460
she was set out to bamboozle us!

07:16.290 --> 07:17.250
No...

07:17.750 --> 07:20.750
From our very first encounter...

07:22.000 --> 07:25.760
She's trying to have fun with me,
perfectly understood what I said!

07:27.610 --> 07:30.100
She can understand human speech?!

07:30.100 --> 07:33.010
She has to. There's no explaining
that reaction otherwise!

07:33.770 --> 07:35.480
Sheesh.

07:35.480 --> 07:40.020
She's a Unique Monster, sure,
but the devs sure put one hell of an AI on her!

07:40.020 --> 07:41.820
What a game, eh?

07:49.300 --> 07:52.160
I shouldn't expect less from
one of the Seven Colossi.

07:52.910 --> 07:54.950
Lycagon the Nightslayer!

07:56.710 --> 08:00.420
There was no way you're just simply
a monster with inflated stats, after all!

08:04.420 --> 08:06.920
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:07.930 --> 08:09.760
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

08:09.760 --> 08:14.810
Well, how do we fight an opponent
as sly as Lycagon?

08:22.500 --> 08:23.650
Vorpal Secret Arts!

08:25.110 --> 08:26.860
Mirror of Fading!

08:26.860 --> 08:28.150
VORPAL SECRET ARTS: MIRROR OF FADING

08:35.200 --> 08:37.330
Sunraku, what's that?

08:37.330 --> 08:39.330
It's kind of a decoy.

08:39.330 --> 08:40.920
It fades away fast, though.

08:41.230 --> 08:45.760
Guess no matter how smart her AI is,
she can't ignore a skill's effect.

08:45.760 --> 08:46.920
I see.

08:47.550 --> 08:50.760
Rei, let's make up a strategy
quick while we can.

08:50.760 --> 08:52.850
A-All right.

08:52.850 --> 08:54.640
That said...

08:54.640 --> 08:58.890
I don't have that many effective
attacks right now, to be honest.

08:59.390 --> 09:03.900
Sunraku, I actually
have an ultimate we can use.

09:03.900 --> 09:05.520
Huh? Ultimate?

09:06.660 --> 09:09.900
The reason I earned
the "Attack Master" moniker.

09:12.370 --> 09:17.540
An attack skill that set the record for
the highest instantaneous damage in SLF.

09:18.540 --> 09:20.370
If I can hit her with it...

09:21.040 --> 09:23.540
I think it will work,
even against Lycagon.

09:23.950 --> 09:26.550
Wow, Rei! You got something like that?!

09:26.550 --> 09:30.050
But the requirement
to use it is quite a pain.

09:30.340 --> 09:35.350
I've never once pulled it off
against Lycagon.

09:36.760 --> 09:39.980
But now, with your help...

09:39.980 --> 09:42.100
It should be doable!

09:43.690 --> 09:44.780
I see.

09:45.210 --> 09:48.320
The Attack Master's ultimate, huh?

09:49.030 --> 09:52.530
I don't think anybody would turn
down such an enticing proposal!

09:54.160 --> 09:55.780
I'm in, Rei.

09:56.620 --> 09:59.330
Let's bet our victory on that!

10:00.450 --> 10:01.210
All right!

10:07.290 --> 10:08.300
Hey!

10:12.110 --> 10:14.490
We're back to battle!

10:16.720 --> 10:18.100
Fleet Float!

10:21.640 --> 10:23.560
Airgetlám!

10:23.980 --> 10:26.440
AIRGETLÁM

10:26.690 --> 10:29.190
BONUS DAMAGE FOR CRITICAL HITS
BASED ON LUCK STAT

10:39.370 --> 10:41.790
One attack ain't enough
to make you flinch, eh?

10:57.090 --> 10:58.600
C'mon, what's wrong?!

10:58.990 --> 11:01.390
You'll never hit me
with those lousy attacks!

11:02.270 --> 11:03.520
To activate this,

11:04.210 --> 11:08.940
I need to land hits with the skills
Apocalypse and Catastrophe,

11:08.940 --> 11:10.520
five times each.

11:10.820 --> 11:14.360
Apocalypse...
That one you used just now, right?

11:14.360 --> 11:15.610
Yes.

11:15.610 --> 11:16.990
SATANAEL
Satanael.

11:16.990 --> 11:17.740
SATANAEL

11:17.740 --> 11:19.740
SATANAEL
It's a Unique Skill that I can use

11:19.740 --> 11:21.410
SATANAEL
while I'm in this form.

11:21.750 --> 11:23.450
And the other one...

11:24.330 --> 11:26.540
Satanael, inverse!

11:27.350 --> 11:28.500
Satan!

11:29.630 --> 11:31.630
SATAN

11:36.680 --> 11:40.100
The Unique Skill I can
only use in Satan form...

11:43.430 --> 11:44.640
Catastrophe!

11:44.640 --> 11:46.770
CATASTROPHE

11:52.520 --> 11:54.320
So that's Catastrophe?

11:54.860 --> 11:59.780
Those skills leave you open before deploying
and easily attract the enemy's attention.

12:00.700 --> 12:02.030
Where are you looking?!

12:02.030 --> 12:03.830
You should be facing me!

12:07.000 --> 12:11.250
That's why I need to keep her
focused on me, more than ever!

12:15.130 --> 12:17.590
Four more times each...

12:17.590 --> 12:20.390
Yeah, it's quite a pain requirement.

12:20.390 --> 12:22.850
But the payoff will be worth
all the effort, right?

12:23.350 --> 12:25.020
I'm counting on you, Rei!

12:25.020 --> 12:27.690
I'll keep Lycagon distracted!

12:27.690 --> 12:28.610
Right!

12:30.980 --> 12:32.980
Sunraku! The moon!

12:32.980 --> 12:34.780
Her invisible clone is coming!

12:34.780 --> 12:36.390
Roger that!

12:40.530 --> 12:42.700
If I can't figure out this attack...

12:43.200 --> 12:45.700
We'll never make it to Rei's ultimate!

12:46.660 --> 12:48.040
Concentrate!

12:48.040 --> 12:52.210
If I can figure out when and where
her invisible clone will attack...

12:52.210 --> 12:54.960
I can dodge it, even if I can't see it!

12:56.630 --> 12:59.970
The moment Lycagon summons her clone...

12:59.970 --> 13:01.970
There's a very soft sound!

13:04.220 --> 13:06.390
I need to listen for that!

13:06.390 --> 13:10.640
Concentrate all my senses to my hearing
and locate the source of the sound!

13:11.980 --> 13:16.230
How the hell can I do that all
while fighting the main one?!

13:24.490 --> 13:25.990
Sunraku!

13:32.120 --> 13:34.170
Argh, dammit!

13:39.550 --> 13:42.050
In the end, I've got to
rely on Inventoria again.

13:42.930 --> 13:44.550
That darn mutt.

13:44.870 --> 13:50.100
She didn't destroy the surrounding
rubble to distract me, did she?

13:50.930 --> 13:55.150
But still, Inventoria eats up too much MP.

13:55.690 --> 13:58.780
Unlike the time with Wethermon
when we were fully prepared,

13:59.280 --> 14:02.320
this battle with Lycagon
kicked off by accident.

14:02.860 --> 14:07.700
I barely prepared, so I don't have
that many healing items on me.

14:16.170 --> 14:19.590
Unless I find a proper solution
against those invisible clones,

14:19.590 --> 14:22.300
it is only a matter of time
before she actually gets to me.

14:22.300 --> 14:24.020
Even the weather's against us?!

14:24.020 --> 14:27.180
What am I supposed to do?! Hang some
Teru Teru Bozu dolls or something?!

14:34.440 --> 14:36.850
Maybe this would work?!

14:46.410 --> 14:50.450
Being in Satan mode
should boost my VIT,

14:50.450 --> 14:53.910
but as it stands,
I'll never have enough healing items!

14:53.910 --> 14:55.830
My bad! I took too long to come back!

14:56.880 --> 14:58.840
Mirror of Reflection!

15:07.850 --> 15:10.640
Sunraku! So you were all right!

15:11.080 --> 15:12.220
What's that headgear?

15:12.850 --> 15:17.420
This? The Non-Standard
Specialized Armor, Adebane...

15:17.980 --> 15:19.900
Adebane's headgear, that is.

15:19.900 --> 15:20.440
NON-STANDARD SPECIALIZED ARMOR: ADEBANE

15:20.440 --> 15:22.940
NON-STANDARD SPECIALIZED ARMOR: ADEBANE
Non-Standard Armor?

15:22.940 --> 15:25.490
Time for a comeback, Rei!

15:25.890 --> 15:28.200
O-Okay.

15:29.100 --> 15:32.290
While it's true that I can't
equip those Sci-Fi suits,

15:32.910 --> 15:35.870
but the headgear is a different story.

15:36.710 --> 15:38.250
And with this helmet...

15:39.750 --> 15:42.420
...and this Non-Standard Ether Reactor...

15:42.420 --> 15:45.800
...I can revive one of Wethermon's relics!

15:48.800 --> 15:51.310
Time for your first job!

15:59.690 --> 16:02.730
Non-Standard Tactical Bird, Suzaku!

16:02.730 --> 16:05.110
NON-STANDARD TACTICAL BIRD
SUZAKU

16:05.110 --> 16:08.680
Non-Standard Tactical Bird... Suzaku?

16:12.830 --> 16:15.540
Oh, the helmet's starting up.

16:15.540 --> 16:16.250
NON-STANDARD TACTICAL BIRD SUZAKU

16:16.250 --> 16:17.540
NON-STANDARD TACTICAL BIRD SUZAKU
Whoa!

16:18.170 --> 16:24.210
The Ether Reactor Beelach repaired
becomes the Tactical Beast's energy core.

16:24.720 --> 16:28.800
And that energy's channeled
into the corresponding powered suit,

16:28.800 --> 16:30.550
releasing its features.

16:31.110 --> 16:32.010
All right!

16:32.390 --> 16:35.850
I was worried that the headgear alone
wouldn't be enough to turn it on,

16:35.850 --> 16:37.810
but looks like we're all good here!

16:38.600 --> 16:42.730
The headgear of Adebane,
the Non-Standard Specialized Armor.

16:42.730 --> 16:47.820
It functions as a way to give command to Suzaku,
the Non-Standard Tactical Bird.

16:48.400 --> 16:51.740
I can finally operate a robot in SLF!

16:51.740 --> 16:54.030
Standby. Requesting orders.

16:55.200 --> 16:56.700
My armaments are as follows...

16:56.700 --> 16:58.040
Hold up there.

16:58.040 --> 17:00.170
Can you save that for later?

17:02.210 --> 17:05.840
Suzaku. There's one thing
I want you to do first.

17:06.710 --> 17:09.090
What's that thing?

17:09.090 --> 17:10.840
A bird robot?

17:11.210 --> 17:15.590
I've been playing SLF for over a year,
but I've never seen that before.

17:19.600 --> 17:21.850
Oh, no. I almost miss
my chance to attack!

17:22.480 --> 17:26.690
I have to land Apocalypse and Catastrophe
five times each...

17:27.190 --> 17:29.150
But I'm still just at one apiece.

17:29.610 --> 17:31.530
I'm being way too careful.

17:31.530 --> 17:34.950
I can't let Sunraku's
effort go to waste.

17:35.490 --> 17:40.500
I've got to satisfy the requirements
and catch up to him!

17:41.080 --> 17:42.500
Catastrophe!

17:47.630 --> 17:50.430
And that's about it.
Can you do it?

17:53.260 --> 17:55.300
Huh? What's up?

17:56.140 --> 17:57.010
Roger.

18:08.440 --> 18:10.610
What's with that pause just now?

18:11.310 --> 18:13.360
It might not be
the flashiest job out there,

18:13.880 --> 18:15.950
but you're the only
one who can do it.

18:16.450 --> 18:18.450
I'm counting on you, Suzaku.

18:21.160 --> 18:22.630
Apocalypse!

18:25.880 --> 18:27.880
Now it's two each!

18:37.640 --> 18:41.390
The decoy is fading out!
I'll get her attention, so step back!

18:41.390 --> 18:42.560
Okay!

18:42.560 --> 18:44.100
RECAST TIME = THE TIME REQUIRED FOR A SKILL
I'll retreat until my recast time is over!

18:44.100 --> 18:45.270
TO BE USABLE AGAIN
I'll retreat until my recast time is over!

18:49.440 --> 18:51.030
What's wrong?

18:51.030 --> 18:53.650
Come at me, Lycagon!

18:59.660 --> 19:01.540
Firing-up!

19:17.970 --> 19:21.140
All right! Time for a comeback!

19:22.640 --> 19:23.890
With the vibration...

19:25.140 --> 19:26.970
Growing-up!

19:38.300 --> 19:42.190
Looks like the head's more susceptible
to damage than the rest of the body!

19:44.160 --> 19:46.540
Hizutome's really amazing.

19:47.540 --> 19:52.300
He's gotten better and better at tracking
Lycagon's moves since the battle began.

19:52.960 --> 19:53.800
But...

19:58.930 --> 20:01.430
Sunraku!
The invisible clones are coming!

20:02.180 --> 20:04.060
The invisible clones are...

20:04.060 --> 20:08.190
...a surprise attack from the darkness
when the moonlight disappears.

20:09.220 --> 20:11.820
That means there's a way to counter that!

20:12.440 --> 20:14.280
You're up!

20:14.280 --> 20:15.520
Suzaku!

20:16.450 --> 20:19.740
Blow away those annoying clouds!

20:19.740 --> 20:21.610
Boosters at maximum output.

20:25.660 --> 20:27.460
Commencing circling maneuvers.

20:35.920 --> 20:38.090
Order accomplished.

20:38.090 --> 20:39.930
Continuing with the mission.

20:40.800 --> 20:41.930
Wow.

20:41.930 --> 20:44.180
The sky is cleared,
revealing the moon.

20:47.770 --> 20:48.990
There you are!

20:48.990 --> 20:53.440
If I can see it, it's not much different
from any other clone attack!

20:55.230 --> 20:57.400
Too bad for you, Lycagon!

20:57.990 --> 21:01.490
Your invisible clones are now
out of commission!

21:01.490 --> 21:03.490
Airgetlám!

21:11.420 --> 21:12.420
Rei!

21:12.420 --> 21:13.250
Yes!

21:14.000 --> 21:17.520
To be honest, I thought we won't
stand a chance against her.

21:18.010 --> 21:21.550
That there was no way we could
put on a fight against Lycagon.

21:22.390 --> 21:23.010
But...

21:23.550 --> 21:24.930
Hizutome...

21:25.260 --> 21:27.770
No matter who we face,
if I'm fighting alongside you...

21:28.850 --> 21:30.310
...I don't feel we can lose!

21:31.690 --> 21:33.400
Apocalypse!

21:42.860 --> 21:43.960
Rei!

23:23.840 --> 23:27.840
But art thou quite sure
that this man is an acquaintance of thy?

23:28.970 --> 23:30.530
I'm not certain.

23:31.220 --> 23:32.350
But...

23:33.020 --> 23:35.380
Based on what Emul told me...

23:35.810 --> 23:37.850
It's the same Sunraku!

23:38.650 --> 23:39.570
I'm sure of it!
